                <pb facs="0181" n="159" sameAs="frus:frus1950v03/pg159"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.5/7–2850: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The United States Deputy Representative on the North
                        Atlantic Council</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Spofford</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">priority</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1950-07-28T23:00:00+01:00">July 28, 1950—11
                            p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p> Depto 20. Report on the fourth session NAC deputies follows: <list>
                        <label>1.</label>
                        <item>Meeting devoted largely discussion US proposal reported Depto 15.
                            Proposal adopted with following amendments: <list>
                                <label>
                                    <hi rendition="#italic">a</hi>.</label>
                                <item>Deletion “European” in first sentence paragraph 3<hi
                                        rendition="#italic">a</hi> proposed by Alphand.</item>
                                <pb facs="0182" n="160" xml:id="pg160"/>
                                <label>
                                    <hi rendition="#italic">b</hi>.</label>
                                <item>Paragraph 3<hi rendition="#italic">b</hi> amended, as
                                    suggested by Alphand, to provide that estimate by standing group
                                    should take into account as far as possible the national efforts
                                    of NAT countries and military aid programs.</item>
                                <label>
                                    <hi rendition="#italic">c</hi>.</label>
                                <item>UK proposed adding to last sentence paragraph 3<hi
                                        rendition="#italic">b</hi> “and the approximate dates by
                                    which they are required.” Amendment accepted on understanding
                                    that its feasibility would be discussed with standing group
                                    representatives.</item>
                                <label>
                                    <hi rendition="#italic">d</hi>.</label>
                                <item>Alphand proposed (supported by UK) amend paragraph 3<hi
                                        rendition="#italic">b</hi> to request SG consideration of
                                    infra-structure. Spofford repeated substance yesterday’s remarks
                                    that study this complicated subject would slow up work on main
                                    project. On understanding that matter would be discussed with
                                    standing group representatives August 1 and would not be
                                    permitted interfere with immediate development of military
                                    production possibilities, following sentence added: “Standing
                                    group shall also be requested to give as soon as feasible an
                                    estimate of infra-structure items of equipment and stocks to be
                                    given similar high priority.”</item>
                                <label>
                                    <hi rendition="#italic">e</hi>.</label>
                                <item>Accepted Alphand amendment deleting words “in Europe” first
                                    sentence paragraph 3<hi rendition="#italic">c</hi> on
                                    understanding US production not to be included in PWS–MPSB
                                    study. UK suggested certain possibilities production in Canada
                                    should be explored and supported Alphand amendment. Spofford
                                    again emphasized immediate problem was to make use unused
                                    military production capacity in Europe.</item>
                                <label>
                                    <hi rendition="#italic">f</hi>.</label>
                                <item>Amended paragraph 3<hi rendition="#italic">d</hi> by
                                    substituting “provisional” for “specific”. Accepted UK amendment
                                    but adding that PWS–DFEC to be requested make an interim report
                                    by August 10. This was substitute for Alphand proposal that
                                    deputies themselves recommend provisional mechanism.</item>
                                <label>
                                    <hi rendition="#italic">g</hi>.</label>
                                <item>Alphand proposed amendment paragraph 3<hi rendition="#italic"
                                        >d</hi> by deleting words “in Europe”. Spofford explained
                                    that if DFEC study was extended to include funds for military
                                    production in North America it could not be expected make useful
                                    report on main subject of study, that is use of European
                                    production capacity. Spofford explained US considering broader
                                    and more flexible forms assistance for additional military
                                    production in Europe and study should concentrate on this
                                    aspect. Alphand withdrew amendment.</item>
                                <label>
                                    <hi rendition="#italic">h</hi>.</label>
                                <item>US proposal approved as amended,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d100-f1"
                                    /> unless any deputy raises objection before 11 a. m., July 29
                                    after receiving clean copies.</item>
                            </list>
                        </item>
                        <label>2.</label>
                        <item>Deputies agreed issue communiqué reported separate Depto 19.<anchor
                                n="2" xml:id="d100-f2"/> As spokesman for deputies, Spofford spoke
                            to press along lines of communiqué.</item>
                        <label>3.</label>
                        <item>Spofford closed meeting with statement urging deputies, in
                            consultation with governments, to stress importance of replies to US
                            inquiries in Depcirctel July 22, 1 a. m.</item>
                    </list>
                </p>
                <pb facs="0183" n="161" xml:id="pg161"/>
                <p>Emphasized that further US actions will depend in large measure on substantial
                    increase in European defense effort.</p>
                <p>Sent Department Depto 20, repeated information Paris 162.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>[<hi rendition="#small-caps">Spofford</hi>]</signed>
                </closer>
